Here's how to handle each scenario in MSTest:

## 1. Windows-Only Tests

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystem.Windows)]
// Or manually:
[TestMethod]
public void RegistryTest()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows");
    // ... registry code
}
```

## 2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("RequiresGPU")]
public void GpuRenderTest()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") == "true")
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI - requires local GPU");
    // ... GPU test
}
```

Filter in CI with: `dotnet test --filter "TestCategory!=RequiresGPU"`

## 3. Flaky External API — Retry

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)] // MSTest 3.x+ built-in retry
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    var result = CallWeatherApi();
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

For older MSTest without `[Retry]`, use a manual loop:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    Exception? last = null;
    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
    {
        try
        {
            var result = CallWeatherApi();
            Assert.IsNotNull(result);
            return; // passed
        }
        catch (Exception ex) { last = ex; Thread.Sleep(1000); }
    }
    Assert.Fail($"Failed after 3 attempts: {last!.Message}");
}
```

## 4. Cleanup Even on Failure

Use `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally`:

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private string? _tempFile;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs even if the test fails
        if (_tempFile != null && File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessTempFileTest()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile!, "data");
        // ... test logic that might throw
    }
}
```

Or inline with `try/finally` for one-off cases:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void SingleTempFileTest()
{
    var path = Path.GetTempFileName();
    try
    {
        File.WriteAllText(path, "test");
        Assert.IsTrue(File.Exists(path));
    }
    finally
    {
        File.Delete(path);
    }
}
```

---

**Summary table:**

| Scenario | Approach |
|----------|----------|
| OS-specific | `Assert.Inconclusive()` or condition attribute |
| Skip in CI | `[TestCategory]` + filter, or env-var check |
| Flaky/retry | `[Retry(n)]` (MSTest 3.x+) |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally` |
